# React Admin Panel Review Checklist

## Architecture Compliance
- [ ] Code follows component-based architecture
- [ ] Proper separation between pages, components, services, and utilities
- [ ] Components are small and focused (< 200 lines)
- [ ] Smart (container) vs presentational component pattern followed
- [ ] Custom hooks extract reusable logic
- [ ] Feature-based organization for related components

## Component Structure
- [ ] Functional components with hooks (no class components)
- [ ] Props properly typed with TypeScript interfaces
- [ ] Prop destructuring in function signature
- [ ] Default prop values provided where appropriate
- [ ] Children prop properly typed (React.ReactNode)
- [ ] Event handlers named with handle prefix (handleClick, handleSubmit)
- [ ] Early returns for conditional rendering

## TypeScript (if applicable)
- [ ] Proper type annotations for props and state
- [ ] No use of `any` type (use specific types or `unknown`)
- [ ] Interfaces defined for complex objects
- [ ] Type/interface exports for reusability
- [ ] Enums or union types for fixed values
- [ ] Generic types used appropriately

## React Hooks
- [ ] useState with proper initial values and types
- [ ] useEffect with correct dependencies array
- [ ] Cleanup functions in useEffect where needed
- [ ] useCallback used for callbacks passed to memoized children
- [ ] useMemo used for expensive calculations
- [ ] useRef used appropriately (DOM refs, mutable values)
- [ ] Custom hooks follow naming convention (use prefix)
- [ ] No missing dependencies (ESLint warnings addressed)

## State Management
- [ ] Local state for component-specific data
- [ ] Context API or Redux for global state
- [ ] State updates are immutable
- [ ] Reducers are pure functions (if using Redux)
- [ ] Action creators properly defined
- [ ] Selectors used to access Redux state
- [ ] No prop drilling (use context or state management)

## API Integration
- [ ] API calls in services, not components
- [ ] Axios interceptors for auth and error handling
- [ ] Loading states handled properly
- [ ] Error states handled and displayed to user
- [ ] API responses properly typed
- [ ] No hardcoded API URLs (use environment variables)

## Performance
- [ ] React.memo used for expensive components
- [ ] useMemo used for expensive calculations
- [ ] useCallback used to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- [ ] Code splitting with React.lazy for routes
- [ ] Suspense boundaries for lazy-loaded components
- [ ] Images optimized and lazy-loaded
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders (check with React DevTools)

## Code Quality
- [ ] Code is free from linting errors (ESLint)
- [ ] Code is formatted consistently (Prettier)
- [ ] No unused variables or imports
- [ ] No console.log statements in production code
- [ ] Proper use of const and let (no var)
- [ ] Arrow functions used appropriately
- [ ] Destructuring used for props and objects
- [ ] Template literals for string concatenation
- [ ] No magic numbers or strings (use constants)

## Error Handling
- [ ] Error boundaries implemented for component trees
- [ ] Try-catch blocks for async operations
- [ ] User-friendly error messages displayed
- [ ] Errors logged appropriately
- [ ] Failed API calls handled gracefully
- [ ] Form validation errors shown clearly

## Forms
- [ ] Form libraries used (React Hook Form or Formik)
- [ ] Input validation implemented
- [ ] Validation errors displayed to user
- [ ] Form submission handled properly
- [ ] Loading states during submission
- [ ] Success/error feedback after submission
- [ ] Disabled state during submission

## Styling
- [ ] SCSS Modules or styled-components used consistently
- [ ] No inline styles (use style objects or classes)
- [ ] Classnames library used for conditional classes
- [ ] Responsive design implemented
- [ ] Consistent spacing and layout
- [ ] Theme variables used for colors, fonts, spacing
- [ ] No hard-coded colors or dimensions

## Routing
- [ ] React Router used for navigation
- [ ] Routes properly defined
- [ ] Protected routes for authenticated pages
- [ ] Route parameters typed and validated
- [ ] Programmatic navigation uses navigate hook
- [ ] 404 page for unknown routes

## Accessibility
- [ ] Semantic HTML elements used
- [ ] ARIA labels where necessary
- [ ] Keyboard navigation supported
- [ ] Focus management handled properly
- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG standards
- [ ] Alt text for images
- [ ] Form inputs have associated labels

## Testing
- [ ] Unit tests for components
- [ ] Tests for custom hooks
- [ ] Integration tests for user flows
- [ ] Tests use React Testing Library
- [ ] Mock API calls in tests
- [ ] Tests cover happy and error paths
- [ ] Meaningful test descriptions

## Security
- [ ] No sensitive data in client-side code
- [ ] XSS prevention (proper escaping)
- [ ] No dangerouslySetInnerHTML without sanitization
- [ ] CSRF tokens for mutations (if applicable)
- [ ] Authentication tokens stored securely
- [ ] No secrets in code (use environment variables)

## Documentation
- [ ] Complex components have JSDoc comments
- [ ] README updated if adding new features
- [ ] Prop types documented for reusable components
- [ ] API service methods documented

