# Flutter Mobile Apps Review Checklist

## Architecture Compliance
- [ ] Code follows feature-based folder structure
- [ ] Screens, widgets, providers, services properly organized
- [ ] Widgets are small and focused
- [ ] Stateless widgets used where possible
- [ ] State management pattern used consistently (Provider/Bloc)

## Widget Structure
- [ ] Widgets properly organized (screens vs widgets)
- [ ] Const constructors used wherever possible
- [ ] Widget lifecycle methods properly implemented
- [ ] Private methods prefixed with underscore
- [ ] Build methods are concise and readable
- [ ] Complex widgets extracted into separate files

## Dart/Flutter Best Practices
- [ ] Strong typing used (no dynamic)
- [ ] Null safety handled properly
- [ ] Named constructors for clarity
- [ ] Factory constructors for JSON parsing
- [ ] copyWith methods for immutable updates
- [ ] Extension methods for enums and models
- [ ] Proper use of final and const

## State Management (Provider)
- [ ] ChangeNotifier classes properly structured
- [ ] notifyListeners() called after state changes
- [ ] Provider properly scoped in widget tree
- [ ] Consumer used for specific rebuilds
- [ ] Provider.of with listen: false for actions
- [ ] No unnecessary rebuilds

## State Management (Bloc - if used)
- [ ] Events, states, and blocs properly defined
- [ ] Bloc pattern followed consistently
- [ ] BlocProvider properly scoped
- [ ] BlocBuilder/BlocConsumer used appropriately
- [ ] State classes are immutable

## Data Models
- [ ] Models properly structured with required fields
- [ ] fromJson and toJson methods implemented
- [ ] copyWith method for immutable updates
- [ ] Equality operators overridden (== and hashCode)
- [ ] toString method overridden for debugging
- [ ] Enums used for fixed values

## API Integration
- [ ] Dio or http package used for API calls
- [ ] API service centralized and organized
- [ ] Interceptors for auth and error handling
- [ ] Error handling for network failures
- [ ] Timeouts configured appropriately
- [ ] Loading states managed properly
- [ ] No hardcoded API URLs

## Performance
- [ ] Const constructors used extensively
- [ ] ListView.builder for long lists
- [ ] Keys used for list items
- [ ] Expensive operations not in build method
- [ ] Images cached (cached_network_image)
- [ ] Proper disposal of controllers and streams
- [ ] No memory leaks

## Navigation
- [ ] Named routes used consistently
- [ ] Route arguments properly typed
- [ ] Navigation properly structured
- [ ] Back button behavior handled
- [ ] Deep linking configured (if needed)

## Code Quality
- [ ] Code is free from analyzer warnings
- [ ] Code is formatted (dartfmt)
- [ ] No unused variables or imports
- [ ] No print statements in production code
- [ ] Meaningful variable and function names
- [ ] Proper indentation and spacing
- [ ] Comments for complex logic

## Error Handling
- [ ] Try-catch blocks for async operations
- [ ] User-friendly error messages
- [ ] Network errors handled gracefully
- [ ] Dio errors properly categorized
- [ ] Loading and error states in UI
- [ ] Snackbars or dialogs for errors

## Forms & Validation
- [ ] Input validation implemented
- [ ] Validation errors displayed
- [ ] Form state managed properly
- [ ] TextEditingController disposed
- [ ] Focus nodes managed correctly
- [ ] Submit button disabled during submission

## Styling & Theming
- [ ] Theme data centralized
- [ ] Colors defined in constants
- [ ] Text styles use Theme.of(context)
- [ ] Consistent spacing (SizedBox, Padding)
- [ ] Responsive design (MediaQuery, LayoutBuilder)
- [ ] Platform-specific UI handled (iOS/Android)

## Platform-Specific
